<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nader Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1736–1747</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Nader Qoli, Nadir Shah, Nader Afshar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nader Shah was a military commander from the Turkic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afshar-tribe">Afshar tribe</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khorasan</a> who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a> and reigned as Shah of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> from 1736 to 1747. Rising in the service of the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a>, he expelled Afghan, Ottoman and Russian occupiers and later sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>, gravely weakening the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>. His punishing taxation and endless campaigns ended in his assassination, after which his realm fragmented and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand Empire</a> emerged.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nader-shah.jpg" alt="Nader Shah" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Contemporary_portrait_of_Nader_Shah._Artist_unknown,_created_in_ca._1740_in_Iran_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
